      "name": "BinkBufferClear",
      "signature": "int BinkBufferClear(BinkBuffer * pBuffer)",
      "comment": "Clears the video data in a Bink buffer by zeroing the pixel data while maintaining proper locking\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock the buffer using BinkBufferLock to ensure exclusive access\n2. If lock succeeds, clear the video buffer using format-specific clearing function\n3. Pass buffer pixel data pointer, dimensions, format, and stride to ClearVideoBufferByFormat\n4. Unlock the buffer to release exclusive access\n5. Return success status (1) if clearing completed\n6. Return failure status (0) if initial lock failed\n\nParameters:\npBuffer (BinkBuffer *): Pointer to Bink video buffer structure containing pixel data and format info\n\nReturns:\n1: Buffer successfully cleared\n0: Failed to lock buffer (buffer may be in use by decoder)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer must be lockable for clearing to proceed - decoder or other processes may prevent locking\n\nBinkBuffer Structure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwFormat         uint    Pixel format identifier  \n0x04    4     dwStride         uint    Bytes per scanline\n0x10    4     dwHeight         uint    Buffer height in pixels\n0x14    4     pbPixelData      byte*   Pointer to pixel data buffer\n0x18    4     dwWidth          uint    Buffer width in pixels",
