      "name": "EnsureDoubleBufferAllocation",
      "signature": "void EnsureDoubleBufferAllocation(int nRequestedSize)",
      "comment": "Ensures double buffer allocation with sufficient capacity for requested size.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 32-byte boundary (add 0x1F and mask with 0xFFFFFFE0)\n2. Calculate total allocation size as aligned size * 2 (for double buffer)\n3. Check if current allocated buffer is smaller than required total size\n4. If reallocation needed:\n   a. Free existing buffer if it exists (g_pBufferBase != NULL)\n   b. Allocate new buffer with RadMalloc using total allocation size\n   c. Update global buffer state: base pointer, allocated size, midpoint pointer\n5. If existing buffer is sufficient, only update midpoint pointer\n6. Set buffer midpoint to base + aligned size (splitting buffer in half)\n\nParameters:\ndwRequestedSize (int): Minimum buffer size required by caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates through global buffer state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero allocation request gets aligned to 32 bytes minimum (0x20)\n- Alignment ensures memory-efficient access patterns for SSE operations\n- Double buffer allows ping-pong operations between first and second half\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1F (31): Alignment mask addition for 32-byte boundary\n0xFFFFFFE0: Alignment mask to clear lower 5 bits (32-byte align)\n2: Double buffer multiplier for total allocation\n\nGlobal Buffer State:\ng_dwBufferAllocatedSize (0x1003C810): Total bytes allocated for buffer\ng_pBufferBase (0x1003C814): Pointer to start of allocated buffer  \ng_pBufferMidpoint (0x1003C818): Pointer to middle of buffer (base + aligned_size)",
