      "name": "BinkGoto",
      "signature": "void BinkGoto(BinkHandle * pBink, uint dwTargetFrame, byte bFlags)",
      "comment": "Seeks to a specific frame in a Bink video file with optional positioning mode control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBink handle is not NULL, exit if invalid\n2. Set busy flag at offset 0x134 to prevent concurrent operations\n3. Clamp dwTargetFrame to maximum frame count if necessary\n4. Check positioning mode flag (bFlags & 0x1):\n   - If direct positioning (bFlags & 0x1): Call BinkPositionFrame directly\n   - If sequential positioning (!(bFlags & 0x1)): Use keyframe-based seeking\n5. For sequential positioning when not already at target frame:\n   - Call BinkGetKeyFrame to find optimal keyframe before target\n   - Compare current frame with target and keyframe positions\n   - If backward seek or keyframe is better, position to keyframe first\n   - Pause video playback during seek operation\n   - Process frames sequentially using BinkDoFrame/BinkNextFrame loop\n   - Continue until current frame equals target frame\n   - Resume playback and clear busy flag\n6. Clear busy flag at offset 0x134 before exit\n\nParameters:\npBink (BinkHandle*): Pointer to Bink video handle structure\ndwTargetFrame (uint): Target frame number to seek to (0-based)\nbFlags (byte): Positioning flags - bit 0 controls seek mode (0=sequential, 1=direct)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, seeking is performed in-place on handle\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf current frame equals target frame, function exits early without processing\nDirect positioning bypasses keyframe optimization for immediate seeking\nSequential positioning ensures proper frame decoding order through keyframes\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x134 (308): Busy flag offset - prevents concurrent Bink operations\n0x8 (8): Frame count offset - maximum frames in video\n0xc (12): Current frame offset - active frame position  \n0x27c (636): Comparison frame offset - used for frame state checking\n0x1: Direct positioning flag mask\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type    Description\n0x8     4     dwFrameCount        uint    Total number of frames in video\n0xc     4     dwCurrentFrame      uint    Currently active frame number\n0x134   4     dwBusyFlag          uint    Concurrent operation prevention flag\n0x27c   4     dwComparisonFrame   uint    Frame state comparison value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6a67f3b3494d555a6ef8df3d0bdf877c"
