      "name": "ConfigureColorProcessingPath",
      "signature": "void ConfigureColorProcessingPath(uint * pProcessingFlags, int nScaleFactor)",
      "comment": "Configure color processing function pointers based on performance timer state and input flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if performance timer has been initialized (g_fPerformanceTimerInitialized == 1)\n2. If not initialized, set function pointers to fallback handlers (LAB_1000cd10, LAB_1000cdd0)\n3. If initialized, validate processing flags from first parameter\n4. Check if flag bit 0 is clear OR flags exceed 0x2000 threshold\n5. If validation fails, set error condition (0x82) and configure error handlers (FUN_1000ce90, FUN_1000cfc0)\n6. If validation passes, calculate new flag value by adding scale factor * 4\n7. Update processing flags with calculated value\n8. Check flag bit 1 to determine processing path\n9. If bit 1 clear, set standard handlers (LAB_1000cbb0, LAB_1000cc60)\n10. If bit 1 set, set alternative handlers (LAB_1000cd10, LAB_1000cdd0)\n\nParameters:\npProcessingFlags - Pointer to uint containing processing flags and state\nnScaleFactor - Integer scale factor for flag calculation (multiplied by 4)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function sets global state via function pointers\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x82 (130) - Error condition flag value set when validation fails\n0x2000 (8192) - Maximum valid flag threshold for processing\n0x1 - Flag validation bit mask (must be set for valid processing)\n0x2 - Processing path selection bit mask\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\nDAT_10036340 - Primary color processing function pointer\nDAT_10036b5c - Secondary color processing function pointer  \nDAT_10038f78 - Processing flags pointer storage\nDAT_10036b50 - Tertiary processing handler pointer\nDAT_10038f70 - Quaternary processing handler pointer\nDAT_10036348 - Processing state flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
