      "name": "InitializeBinkTiming",
      "signature": "void InitializeBinkTiming(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder)",
      "comment": "Initialize timing state for Bink video decoder if not already set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if timestamp field (offset 0x20c) is zero (uninitialized)\n2. If uninitialized, get current system time using timeGetTime API\n3. Store current time at offset 0x20c as initial timestamp\n4. Decrement frame count from offset 0x1fc and store at offset 0x210\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder - BinkDecoder * - Pointer to Bink decoder structure containing timing state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf timestamp is already initialized (non-zero), function returns immediately without modification\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description\n0x1fc  | 4    | frameCount    | int  | Current frame number\n0x20c  | 4    | timestamp     | uint | Timing reference point (milliseconds)\n0x210  | 4    | prevFrameNum  | int  | Previous frame number (frameCount - 1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x20c (524) - Offset to timestamp field in BinkDecoder structure\n0x1fc (508) - Offset to frame count field in BinkDecoder structure  \n0x210 (528) - Offset to previous frame number field in BinkDecoder structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4c594ffa40cc6011fbd055a26c7a7a9c"
