      "name": "InitializeBitCountStructure",
      "signature": "void InitializeBitCountStructure(uint dwSourceValue, BitCountInfo * pBitInfo, int nBaseOffset, uint dwShiftAmount, uint dwBitPosition, int nMultiplier, int nEnableBitMask)",
      "comment": "Initializes a BitCountInfo structure with bit count calculations and bit manipulation values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Calculate lookup index using: baseOffset + (shiftAmount >> 3) * multiplier\n2. Determine bit count using hierarchical range checking:\n   - Range 0-128: Use lookup table at g_abBitCountLookupTable[index]\n   - Range 129-2047: Calculate based on sub-ranges with constants 9-11\n   - Range 2048-8191: Calculate based on sub-ranges with constants 13-14\n   - Range 8192+: Calculate based on sub-ranges with constants 15\n3. Store calculated bit count in pBitInfo->bitCount (offset 0x28)\n4. Initialize structure fields: clear first two DWORDs, set bitPosition\n5. Conditionally set bit mask based on enableBitMask parameter:\n   - If enabled: Calculate power-of-2 mask using (1 << (bitPosition-1))\n   - If disabled: Set bit mask to 0\n6. Store sourceValue in pBitInfo->sourceValue (offset 0x2c)\n\nParameters:\n\ndwSourceValue (uint): Source value to store in structure\npBitInfo (BitCountInfo *): Pointer to output structure for bit count information\nnBaseOffset (int): Base offset for lookup table indexing\ndwShiftAmount (uint): Value to right-shift by 3 bits for index calculation\ndwBitPosition (uint): Bit position value to store and use for mask calculation\nnMultiplier (int): Multiplier for scaled index calculation\nnEnableBitMask (int): Flag to enable/disable bit mask calculation (0=disable, non-zero=enable)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - Function modifies pBitInfo structure in-place",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:623afa8601b5f4e2ac2f66474834215c"
