      "name": "InverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8",
      "signature": "void InverseDiscreteCosineTransform8x8(int nOutputWidth, int nOutputStride, short * pInputBlock, int * pCoefficientTable)",
      "comment": "Performs 8x8 Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform using integer arithmetic with fixed-point precision\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output pointers based on stride and width parameters \n2. Loop through 8 columns, processing frequency coefficients to spatial domain\n3. For each column, check if high-frequency coefficients are zero (DC-only optimization)\n4. If DC-only: multiply DC coefficient by first table entry, right-shift by 11 bits, replicate to all 8 rows\n5. If full transform needed: apply 1D IDCT using coefficient table with complex butterfly operations\n6. Store intermediate results in 16-word transform buffer with proper indexing\n7. Loop through 8 rows, performing second 1D IDCT on transposed data\n8. Apply final butterfly transforms with rotation constants (0xb50, 0xec8, 0x8a9, -0x14e8)\n9. Pack results with rounding (+0x7f), right-shift by 8 bits, clamp to 8-bit range\n10. Duplicate packed pixels and store to dual output locations with stride advancement\n\nParameters:\nnOutputWidth - Width dimension for calculating output buffer addresses\nnOutputStride - Byte stride between output rows for proper 2D addressing  \npInputBlock - Pointer to 8x8 block of frequency coefficients (16-bit signed values)\npCoefficientTable - Pointer to 64-entry IDCT coefficient lookup table (32-bit integers)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (results written directly to output buffer locations)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nDC-only optimization when high-frequency coefficients [1-7] are all zero\nUses separable transform: column transform followed by row transform\nFixed-point arithmetic with 11-bit fractional precision for coefficients\nFinal output uses 8-bit precision with rounding and clamping\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xb50 (2896) - Cosine coefficient for rotation angle \u03c0/8 * 2^11 precision\n0xec8 (3784) - Cosine coefficient for 3\u03c0/8 rotation * 2^11 precision  \n0x8a9 (2217) - Sine coefficient for \u03c0/8 rotation * 2^11 precision\n-0x14e8 (-5352) - Negative sine coefficient for 3\u03c0/8 rotation * 2^11 precision\n0x7f (127) - Rounding constant for 8-bit conversion (128/2 - 1)\n0xb (11) - Right-shift amount for coefficient fixed-point to integer conversion\n0x8 (8) - Right-shift amount for final 8-bit output conversion",
