      "name": "BinkCloseMiles",
      "signature": "void BinkCloseMiles(BINK * pBink)",
      "comment": "Closes Miles Sound System resources associated with a BINK video handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Extract Miles audio handle from BINK structure at offset 0x3c\n2. Call first Miles close function with extracted handle\n3. Extract Miles secondary handle from BINK structure at offset 0x44  \n4. Call second Miles close function with secondary handle\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n\npBink - Pointer to BINK video structure containing Miles handles\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\n- Function assumes both Miles function pointers are valid (no null checks)\n- Handles at offsets 0x3c and 0x44 are passed directly without validation\n- Miles close functions are called via global function pointers\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x3c (60) - Offset to primary Miles audio handle in BINK structure\n0x44 (68) - Offset to secondary Miles audio handle in BINK structure\n\nError Handling:\n\n- No error handling - assumes valid BINK pointer and initialized Miles handles\n- Relies on Miles Sound System functions for internal error handling",
