      "name": "RadMalloc",
      "signature": "int RadMalloc(uint dwSize)",
      "comment": "Allocate aligned memory block with 32-byte boundary alignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input size parameter (non-zero, not 0xffffffff sentinel value)\n2. Call _malloc() with requested size plus 0x20 alignment padding bytes\n3. Calculate alignment offset needed to align result to 32-byte boundary\n4. Store alignment offset in byte immediately before aligned address\n5. Return aligned memory address for user allocation\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Requested memory size in bytes, must be non-zero and not 0xffffffff\n\nReturns:\n- Success: Aligned memory address (32-byte boundary aligned)\n- Failure: 0 if dwSize is invalid or _malloc() fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic Values: 0xffffffff treated as invalid size sentinel\n- Alignment: 32-byte boundary alignment (0x20) using offset calculation\n- Storage: Alignment offset stored at [aligned_addr - 1] for deallocation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x20 (32): Alignment boundary and padding size\n- 0x1f (31): Alignment mask for offset calculation  \n- 0xffffffff: Invalid size sentinel value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ccf71b7c6bd67f4220ac02d284da0560"
