      "name": "RadFree",
      "signature": "void RadFree(uint dwMemory)",
      "comment": "Frees memory allocated by RAD custom memory allocator\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is not null\n2. Read allocation size byte stored at dwMemory-1 \n3. Calculate actual allocation base address by subtracting size from pointer\n4. Call system deallocation function with base address\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\ndwMemory (uint): Pointer to user data (not allocation base). May be null.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer handling: Function safely handles null input by early return\n- Allocation format: Uses custom prefix format where size byte precedes user data\n- Memory layout: [size_byte][user_data...] where dwMemory points to user_data\n\nMemory Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field          Type    Description  \n-1      1     allocation_size byte   Size of original allocation block\n0       N     user_data      varies  Actual user data pointed to by dwMemory",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ce7b7bb0113fd49b4bbcff6f485c13e8"
