      "name": "BinkSetVideoOnOff",
      "signature": "void BinkSetVideoOnOff(BinkContext * pBinkContext, DWORD bVideoEnabled)",
      "comment": "Enables or disables video output for a Bink video context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate Bink context pointer is not NULL\n2. Store video enable flag at offset 0x230 in context structure\n3. Return without error indication\n\nParameters:\n  pBinkContext (BinkContext*): Pointer to Bink video playback context structure\n  bVideoEnabled (DWORD): Video enable flag (0=disable video, non-zero=enable video)\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value or error indication\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pBinkContext is NULL, function returns without action (silent failure)\n  - Function does not validate bVideoEnabled parameter value\n  - No error reporting mechanism for invalid context\n\nStructure Layout:\n  BinkContext:\n    Offset  Size  Field Name     Type   Description\n    0x000   560   reserved       byte[] Reserved/unknown fields\n    0x230   4     videoEnabled   DWORD  Video output enable flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
