      "name": "BinkCloseTrack",
      "signature": "void BinkCloseTrack(BinkTrack * pTrack)",
      "comment": "Closes and deallocates a Bink audio track structure and its associated buffers\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate track pointer is not null\n2. Check if audio buffer pointer at offset 0x14 exists\n3. Free audio buffer using FUN_1001a500 (which calls RadFree)\n4. Clear audio buffer pointer to null\n5. Free the track structure itself using RadFree\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npTrack (BinkTrack *): Pointer to track structure to close and deallocate. May be null.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer handling: Function safely handles null pTrack by early return\n- Double-free protection: Audio buffer pointer is cleared after deallocation\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type     Description\n0x00    20    field_0x00     byte[20] Reserved data or metadata fields  \n0x14    4     pAudioBuffer   void*    Pointer to allocated audio buffer data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:de598d52c0612751d3d66fac812e7e95"
