      "name": "CalculateBundleSize",
      "signature": "uint CalculateBundleSize(int nBlockCount, uint dwBaseSize, uint dwElementSize, int nMultiplier)",
      "comment": "Calculates aligned buffer size for data bundle allocation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Normalize element size: set minimum of 8 bytes or snap to 16 bytes if between 9-15\n2. Calculate base allocation: (dwBaseSize >> 3) * dwElementSize * nMultiplier >> 3  \n3. Calculate block overhead: nBlockCount * dwElementSize >> 3\n4. Add 3 bytes padding and align to 4-byte boundary with mask 0xfffffffc\n\nParameters:\nnBlockCount - number of data blocks to allocate space for\ndwBaseSize - base size value used in allocation calculation (typically 512/0x200)\ndwElementSize - size in bytes of individual data elements (4, 5, 8, 11)\nnMultiplier - scaling factor applied to base calculation (1, 8, 48, 64)\n\nReturns:\nuint - calculated buffer size in bytes, aligned to 4-byte boundary\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Element sizes 1-8 normalized to 8 bytes minimum\n- Element sizes 9-15 snapped up to 16 bytes exactly  \n- Result includes 3-byte padding before 4-byte alignment\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 (8) - minimum element size enforced\n0x10 (16) - snap target for medium element sizes (9-15 bytes)\n0x3 (3) - padding bytes added before alignment\n0xfffffffc - 4-byte alignment mask (clears low 2 bits)",
