      "name": "BinkBufferSetHWND",
      "signature": "int BinkBufferSetHWND(BinkBuffer * pBinkBuffer, HWND hWnd)",
      "comment": "Stub implementation for setting window handle for Bink video buffer operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear EAX register to establish success return value\n2. Return immediately without parameter validation or processing\n3. Clean up 8 bytes from stack (__stdcall convention)\n\nParameters:\npBinkBuffer - Pointer to BinkBuffer structure containing video buffer state (unused in stub)\nhWnd - Window handle (HWND) to associate with video buffer for rendering operations (unused in stub)\n\nReturns:\n0 - Always returns success status indicating operation completed\nFunction acts as compatibility stub without implementing actual window association\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a stub implementation providing API compatibility for Bink video library.\nReal implementation would validate buffer pointer, check window handle validity,\nand configure buffer for window-specific video rendering operations. Current stub\nallows applications to call this function without errors while providing no functionality.",
